      "source": "// priority_queue — contest idiom (reference, uses the standard library).\n// C++17, headers <functional> <queue> <vector>. push/pop O(log n), top O(1); top()/pop() on an empty queue is UB.\n// Default is a MAX-heap. Min-heap: third template argument std::greater<T>. Pair keys compare lexicographically.\n#include <functional>\n#include <queue>\n#include <vector>\ntemplate <class T>\nusing MinPQ = std::priority_queue<T, std::vector<T>, std::greater<T>>;\n// Pops everything, returns the values in non-increasing order (heap sort via the queue).\nstd::vector<int> drain_desc(std::vector<int> v) {\n  std::priority_queue<int> pq(v.begin(), v.end());\n  std::vector<int> out;\n  while (!pq.empty()) out.push_back(pq.top()), pq.pop();\n  return out;\n}\n\n// ---- example main (stdin/stdout): line 1: n; line 2: n ints. Prints them in non-increasing order, space separated.\n#include <cstdio>\nint main() {\n  int n;\n  if (std::scanf(\"%d\", &n) != 1) return 0;\n  std::vector<int> v(n);\n  for (int& x : v) std::scanf(\"%d\", &x);\n  std::vector<int> r = drain_desc(v);\n  for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) std::printf(\"%d%c\", r[i], i + 1 < n ? ' ' : '\\n');\n  return 0;\n}\n",
